nodecode-jina is a rewrite of Adolanium's Adolanium/hermes-jina:

  https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-jina
  commit 98505951a3d26230dc30dfd47a502fcdc396f793
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Adolanium (LICENSE)

The plugin was one Python module: a web backend registered through its
harness' provider API, so the harness' own web_extract and web_search calls
were routed to Jina Reader (POST https://r.jina.ai/) and Jina Search (GET
https://s.jina.ai/) when the operator chose it. It added no tools of its own.
This rewrite keeps both operations and every decision the plugin made about
them — the anonymous Reader works without a key while search requires one, a
key rides as a bearer token to Jina only, only http and https urls are sent,
images are dropped from the Markdown, search answers snippets rather than
page content and at most 20 of them, one broken url in a batch fails alone,
and a refused call names the status and Jina's own message. The two
operations are the cell's two tools, called through nlk:http, so no Python,
no harness provider API and no backend switch are needed. What was left out:
the backend selection itself (a cell is present or absent), the parallel
reads the plugin did two or five urls at a time (this cell reads them in
turn), and the harness' per-profile secret scope, which a Nodecode section
replaces. Nothing of the original is vendored.
